From f65aa66fea95210895b9d3303fa9059ce86812e5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: salvamalfa <salvamalfas@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 14 Sep 2026 03:16:29 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 01/19] Add research on passengers by airline and domestic
 route

Investigate whether a passengers-by-airline-and-route breakdown can be
obtained for Mexican domestic flights, checking each candidate source by
opening the file rather than relying on its description.

Findings:
- No free public source crosses route and airline for domestic Mexico.
  AFAC publishes the two marginals separately: the origin-destination
  workbook (sase) has no airline column, and the airline workbook
  (resumen) has no origin/destination in any of its nine sheets.
- The underlying cube does exist: over 2025Q1 the route totals sum to
  14,799,004 passengers against 14,799,050 from the airline bulletin, a
  46-passenger gap (0.0003%), so both publications derive from the same
  microdata. Article 84 of the Ley de Aviacion Civil requires airlines to
  file monthly and AFAC to publish quarterly.
- The marginals do not identify the joint distribution: two distinct route
  subsets sum exactly to the reported Aerus quarterly total.

Deliverables: verified figures for Tijuana-Uruapan (single-operator route),
the Mexico-Cancun trunk total without an obtainable split, a BTS T-100
contrast where the same table is fully verifiable, the route to obtain the
rest via a transparency request, and an explicit list of what could not be
verified.

Also adds the extracted 2025Q1 origin-destination dataset (1,581 rows).

